# {status, user, review, reason}): DRAFT to OPEN, OPEN to SETTLED, DRAFT, OPEN or PENDING to VOID,
# and SETTLED to VOID by a steward within 7 days of its settling (its status log's SETTLED date); DRAFT
# to DELETED (deleted: it counts nowhere), and DELETED back to DRAFT (restored) only on the sheet's today it
# was deleted on (its status log's last DELETED date).
# A clerk (any user not assigned steward) settling a claim whose due is above the sheet's clerk limit
# sends it to PENDING instead. A steward reviews a PENDING claim (review true): status SETTLED approves
# it (not by the user who opened it or last edited it), status OPEN with a reason rejects it. Refused (400) for any
# other change, when the sheet's permission matrix (perm-open, perm-settle, perm-void; by default a
# clerk or a steward) does not allow the user's role to open, settle or void, when settling or approving a claim with no proofs whose due is above the proof threshold
# in force on its date, when opening a claim with an empty note whose due is above the note threshold
# in force on its date (both checked before the clerk limit, so it never goes to PENDING), when the user who opened the claim or last edited it (claim form or amount entry) tries to settle or approve it, when the claim is not on
# the sheet, or when its due-by falls in a closed period, or when opening a DRAFT whose due-by falls in a period
# with a cap while its person already has that many OPEN or PENDING claims due in it; nothing is stored then. Opening records the
# user as the claim's opened-by; a claim whose due is above the review threshold in force on its date goes to REVIEW (no
# number yet, CLAIM_REVIEW) instead of OPEN, and only a steward's review (status OPEN, review true) moves it on: CLAIM_REVIEWED,
# then CLAIM_OPENED with its number. A REVIEW claim may otherwise only be voided.
# A stored change is recorded in the audit file as CLAIM_OPENED,
# CLAIM_PENDING, CLAIM_SETTLED, CLAIM_APPROVED, CLAIM_REJECTED, CLAIM_VOIDED, CLAIM_DELETED or CLAIM_RESTORED (with reversed=<the
# frozen figure> when a SETTLED claim is voided). While the sheet has void reasons, a void needs one of
# them as its reason (refused otherwise); it is kept on the claim and CLAIM_VOIDED ends with reason=<it>.
# A settle may name a date (on, yyyy-MM-dd): its due is then frozen as the claim stood at the end of that date (the
# as-of view, the date standing in for the sheet's today), and CLAIM_SETTLED ends with on=<date>; refused when the
